From a143c7e24f62139f7de5e060b787987e73937ac7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moto <j3tm0t0@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:14:56 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] netpipe: crypto accelerator (X25519/Ed25519 on the Pico) via
 control records in the X6NR stream

The X68000 Z's SSH client (dropbear, 68000 @ 10MHz) spends ~59 s of a 65 s
handshake in Curve25519/Ed25519. Records whose first payload byte is 0xA5
(not an IPv4 version nibble, so old firmware/npd.x skip them) carry a
request (op, id, scalar/point/key/signature/message) from the Z; a FreeRTOS
task computes it with Monocypher 4.0.2 (vendored under src/monocypher, CC0 /
BSD-2) and np_exchange puts the response record first in the next exchange.
One request in flight; a repeated identical request is answered from the
cached result; a request during computation gets ACCEL_ST_BUSY.

Ops: PING (caps), X25519, X25519_BASE (keygen), ED25519_VERIFY, ED25519_SIGN.
Message cap 1024 bytes (ssh needs 32 for the hostkey check, ~200 for the
userauth signature). Shared header accel_proto.h and accel_ops.c are the
same files as x68k's net/accel (host-tested against RFC 7748/8032 vectors
and python cryptography).

text +36.7KB, bss +2.4KB; task stack 6KB (deepest path measured 2.1KB).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01S5R6WJAV75Fci9XiiCqM54
